# bashmaps — transit directions via Google Routes API

## chain
input.txt → bashmaps.sh → write_request.py → request.json → curl Routes API
→ response.json → write_steps.py → steps.json → write_result.py → result.txt
→ server.py writes result.html → browser

## scripts

# bashmaps.sh
— main orchestrator. Reads input.txt (format: origin.destination.DEP|ARR HHMM),
parses the input string, builds an ISO 8601 timestamp, calls write_request.py to update
request.json, POSTs to the Google Routes API, then pipes the response through write_steps.py
(intermediate JSON) and write_result.py (plain text) to produce result.txt.
Short walk steps under 30m are filtered from the output.

# server.py
— lightweight HTTP server (Python stdlib only).
Serves input.html and result.html, handles form POST from input.html,
runs the bashmaps.sh pipeline, and writes result.html from result.txt.
Also serves a dynamic /admin page for managing city and location favourites in config.json.
GET  /              — serve result.html
GET  /input.html    — serve input.html
GET  /admin         — dynamic admin page
POST /query         — run bashmaps.sh pipeline
POST /admin/city    — update _CITY in config.json
POST /admin/geocode — geocode address or AT stop code, serve confirm page
POST /admin/code    — store confirmed value in config.json
POST /admin/delete  — remove favourite from config.json

# write_request.py
— builds request.json for the Google Routes API. Reads origin, destination,
type (DEP|ARR) and timestamp from bashmaps.sh. Resolves locations against config.json:
place IDs (ChIJ...), lat/lng coordinates, or address strings get appropriate API formats;
unrecognised tokens get the default city and country appended. Mode, routing preference
and city default are also read from config.json.

# write_steps.py
— reads response.json, extracts transit and walk steps, converts times to 24hr,
writes structured intermediate JSON to steps.json.

# write_result.py
— reads steps.json, formats as plain text to result.txt.
Transit legs as two-line summaries (dep/arr times leading).
Walk steps included; short walks under 30m filtered in bashmaps.sh.

## files
# config.json   — user config and favourites, managed via /admin
# input.html    — web query form
# result.html   — generated at runtime by server.py from result.txt (not in git)
# request.json  — JSON sent in curl request [write_request.py]
# response.json — raw Routes API response [bashmaps.sh]
# steps.json    — useful subset of response.json [write_steps.py]
# result.txt    — human-friendly plain text [write_result.py]
# input.txt     — current query string [testing/form POST]

## utils/
# add_fav.sh   — geocode address, confirm via Maps link, store to config.json

## not in git
# .env          — GMAPS_API_KEY, PORT


